wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(7651568834029375749)
,p_plug_name=>'Deployment in Oracle APEX'
,p_static_id=>'deployment-in-oracle-apex'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-Region--hideShowIconsMath:t-Region--controlsPosEnd:is-expanded:t-Region--stacked:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>2665811232373458102
,p_plug_display_sequence=>30
,p_plug_item_display_point=>'ABOVE'
,p_location=>null
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p> Deployment is the process of moving an application from development to testing and production environments. Oracle recommends using separate instances for development, testing, and production as a best practice. </p>',
'<ul>',
'<p><strong><h4 style="text-decoration: underline;"> Core Deployment Method: Export/Import</h4></strong></p>',
'    <li> <strong> Export the Application: </strong> In the development environment''s App Builder, the application and its associated components are exported into a single SQL script file.</li><br>',
'    <li> <strong> Transfer the File: </strong> The SQL file is moved to the target environment (test or production).</li><br>',
'    <li> <strong> Import and Install: </strong> In the target environment''s App Builder or using a command-line tool, the SQL script is imported and installed. During import, you can map the application to a different schema or change the application'
||' ID if needed.  </li>',
'</ul>',
'',
'<ul>',
'<p><strong><h4 style="text-decoration: underline;"> Advanced Deployment Options </h4></strong></p>',
'    <li> <strong> Version Control & CI/CD: </strong> APEX applications can be integrated with version control systems (e.g., Git) by splitting the exported SQL file into individual component files. Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD)'
||' pipelines can be set up using tools like Jenkins, Gradle, and Liquibase to automate the build, test, and deployment processes.</li><br>',
'    <li> <strong> One-Click Remote Deployment: </strong> This feature allows deploying an application to a remote APEX instance using configured REST Enabled SQL references, simplifying the process for connected environments.</li><br>',
'    <li> <strong> Deployment Flexibility: </strong> APEX applications are highly portable and can be deployed wherever an Oracle Database runs, including:',
'    <ol>',
'        <li><strong> Oracle Cloud (OCI): </strong> Fully managed services like Autonomous Transaction Processing or the specialized APEX Application Development (APEX Service).</li>',
'        <li><strong> On-Premises: </strong> In a company''s own data center.</li>',
'        <li><strong> Third-Party Clouds: </strong> Major clouds like AWS or Azure that run an Oracle Database instance.</li>      ',
'    </ol>',
'    </li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(7651568619443375747)
