'Application Processes are used to execute PL/SQL code at the application level. These processes are not limited to a single page and can run globally based on defined conditions or events. They help developers perform background operations and contro'
||'l application behavior.',
'</p>',
'',
'<p>To access the Application Processes page:</p>',
'',
'<ol>',
'  <li>On the Workspace home page, click the <strong>App Builder</strong> icon.</li>',
'  ',
'  <li>Select the application.<br>',
'      The Application home page appears.',
'  </li>',
'  ',
'  <li>Click <strong>Shared Components</strong>.</li>',
'  ',
'  <li>Under <strong>Application Logic</strong>, click <strong>Application Processes</strong>.</li>',
'  ',
'  <li>Click the <strong>Create</strong> button.</li>',
'  ',
'  <li>Select the process type and click <strong>Next</strong>.</li>',
'  ',
'  <li>Enter the required details such as:<br>',
'      <strong>Name</strong><br>',
'      <strong>Process Point</strong><br>',
'      <strong>PL/SQL Code</strong>',
'  </li>',
'  ',
'  <li>Click <strong>Apply Changes</strong> to save your changes.</li>',
'</ol>',
'',
